1
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:53,500
In order to trap him, he must become him.

2
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Face/Off is a action, crime, science fiction film directed by John Woo.

3
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:28,500
In order to foil a terrorist plot, an FBI agent undergoes facial transplant
surgery and assumes the identity of a criminal mastermind.

4
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:16,000
The plan turns sour when the criminal wakes up prematurely and seeks revenge.

5
00:28:57,500 --> 00:29:03,500
Sean Archer, played by John Travolta.

6
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:51,000
Castor Troy, played by Nicolas Cage.

7
00:40:32,500 --> 00:40:38,500
Eve Archer, played by Joan Allen.

8
00:46:20,000 --> 00:46:26,000
Pollux Troy, played by Alessandro Nivola.

9
00:52:07,500 --> 00:52:13,500
Sasha Hassler, played by Gina Gershon.

10
00:57:55,000 --> 00:58:01,000
Jamie Archer, played by Dominique Swain.

11
01:03:42,500 --> 01:03:48,500
Face/Off is a 1997 American science fiction action thriller film directed by
John Woo, from a screenplay by Mike Werb and Michael Colleary.

12
01:09:30,000 --> 01:09:36,000
It stars John Travolta as an FBI agent and Nicolas Cage as a terrorist, who
undergo an experimental surgery to swap their faces and identities.

13
01:15:17,500 --> 01:15:23,500
The film co-stars Joan Allen, Gina Gershon, and Alessandro Nivola in his film debut, and features Dominique
Swain, Nick Cassavetes, Harve Presnell, Colm Feore, CCH Pounder, and Thomas Jane in supporting roles.

14
01:21:05,000 --> 01:21:11,000
Principal photography began on January 4, 1997 in
Los Angeles and wrapped on April 1.

15
01:26:52,500 --> 01:26:58,500
The film score was composed by John Powell.

16
01:32:40,000 --> 01:32:46,000
It was the first Hollywood film in which Woo was given major creative control.

17
01:38:27,500 --> 01:38:33,500
Face/Off was theatrically released on June 27, 1997 in the United States by Paramount Pictures and
internationally by Buena Vista International through its Touchstone Pictures banner.

18
01:44:15,000 --> 01:44:21,000
It earned critical acclaim for the performances by Cage and
Travolta and its stylized action sequences.

19
01:50:02,500 --> 01:50:08,500
Face/Off earned $245.7 million worldwide on a $80 million budget,
making it the 11th highest-grossing film of 1997.

20
01:55:50,000 --> 01:55:56,000
At the 70th Academy Awards, it was nominated for Best Sound Effects Editing.

21
02:01:37,500 --> 02:01:43,500
Over the years since its release, Face/Off has gained a cult
following and is considered as one of Woo's best films.

22
02:07:25,000 --> 02:07:31,000
The film explores themes of prison, biological
weapon, prisoner, bomb, undercover.

23
02:13:12,500 --> 02:13:18,500
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
